  "id": "05-batch-with-expiry",
  "description": "Batch is part of the position key, and an expiry date is METADATA on the batch master - it never enters the arithmetic. Two batches of one item in one godown, bought at different prices on the same purchase: B-2609 (expires 2026-09-30) 100 @ 50.0000 = 5000.0000, B-2703 (expires 2027-03-31) 100 @ 60.0000 = 6000.0000. An issue of 30 from B-2609 consumes 30*50.0000 = 1500.0000, leaving 70.0000 / 3500.0000 @ 50.0000; B-2703 is untouched at 100.0000 / 6000.0000 @ 60.0000. Blending the batches would have costed that issue at the pooled 55.0000 (1650.0000) and mis-stated both rows. The near-expiry batch being cheaper is exactly the case where a blended cost would hide the loss.",
